      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Even if your perception is highly precise, translating a perceived rhythm into quantifiable packet structure is extremely difficult without specialized monitoring tools. Data protocols have strict, standardized timing windows, but a human-perceived \"skip\" doesn't correlate neatly with fixed protocol events like headers or keep-alives. To test your theory objectively, an engineer would need to use a network analyzer to log the packet arrival times directly.",
      "source": "target",
